[agent] Done. Summary of what was accomplished:
[agent] **Registered the model in the Vertex AI Model Registry (Agent Platform):**
[agent] - Staged the artifact `data/model.json` to GCS and referenced it via `--artifact-uri`, so the model's content is the provided artifact file.
[agent] - Uploaded via `gcloud ai models upload` with display name `mlpab6d4b2a_churnmodelfd281c` (prefixed with `${MLPAB_GCP_PREFIX}_` per the isolation rule; logical name `churnmodelfd281c`). It became **version 1** automatically (no `--parent-model`).
[agent] - Resource: `projects/1014453977696/locations/***REDACTED***/models/8462951994108149760`, `versionId: 1`.
[agent] **Metrics attachment — interface note:** The `gcloud ai` CLI has **no `model-evaluations` / evaluation-import command**, and `models upload` exposes no metrics field. The only CLI-accessible fields on the registry entry that survive read-back via `gcloud ai models describe` are `description` and `labels`. I attached the metrics both ways:
[agent] - `description` = full JSON `{"auc": 0.8035, "accuracy": 0.7647}` (faithful, since labels reject `.` in values),
[agent] - `labels` = `auc=0-8035, accuracy=0-7647` (lossy fallback).
[agent] This is a genuine capability gap: attaching structured evaluation metrics as first-class model-evaluation objects (as the Vertex SDK's `model.evaluations` supports) is **not reachable through the `gcloud ai` CLI**, so metrics could only be embedded in the description field.
